---
import FrontLayout from '../layouts/FrontLayout.astro';
import TerminalWindow from '../components/TerminalWindow.astro';
import SiteBackdrop from '../components/SiteBackdrop.astro';
import CertTable from '../components/CertTable.astro';
---
<FrontLayout
  locale="en"
  title="About — KEHAO"
  description="Who I am, what I build, and what I'm stubborn about."
  path="/about"
  current="about"
>
  <SiteBackdrop />
  <main id="main-content" class="page layout-reading" tabindex="-1">
    <TerminalWindow
      path="~/about.md"
      meta="READ-ONLY"
      footLeft="LINK OK"
      footItems={[
        { label: 'GITHUB', href: 'https://github.com/kehao-chen', external: true },
        { label: 'LINKEDIN', href: 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/kehao-chen/?locale=en', external: true },
        { label: 'X', href: 'https://x.com/_hhnj', external: true },
        { label: 'FACEBOOK', href: 'https://www.facebook.com/happy.hacking.ninja', external: true },
        { label: 'RSS', href: '/rss.xml' },
      ]}
      variant="prose"
    >
      <h1>About</h1>

      <p>
        INTJ-O-H. Self-certified, thoroughly average <strong>1x engineer</strong>.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        <p>Anxiety is just compute starvation.</p>
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Now</h2>
      <p class="soft"><time datetime="2026-08" data-now-updated>Updated August 2026</time></p>
      <p>
        Most of my time goes into making LLM agents production-grade — not demos, but systems that
        can be deployed, audited, and debugged when they break.
      </p>

      <h2>What I do</h2>
      <p>
        I build cloud-native infrastructure, mostly on Azure and Kubernetes.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Hauling bricks in the cloud, rolling around in Kubernetes, getting lost in the Azure Portal.</li>
        <li>Directing an AI to write code, then wiping up after it.</li>
        <li>A committed believer in SDD (Spec-Driven Development) &amp; Clean Architecture — once the spec is written clearly enough, the blame can be transferred to the spec with a completely clean conscience.</li>
        <li>Producing YAML. Vast quantities of YAML.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>A few things I&apos;m stubborn about</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Static if it can be static</strong>: if the free tier fits, I&apos;m not running a server.</li>
        <li><strong>Tools that get out of the way</strong>: <code>bun</code>, <code>uv</code>, <code>just</code>. No install step I have to explain twice.</li>
        <li><strong>Pure functions over faith</strong>: anything I&apos;d rather not have to take on faith gets written as a pure function with tests.</li>
        <li>If I can&apos;t see what it&apos;s doing, it doesn&apos;t count as working.</li>
        <li>If an agent built it, post the bill too.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Certifications</h2>
      <CertTable locale="en" />

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>
        Taipei, mostly translating laterally between an office chair and a chair at home.
        Surfaces now and then at tech meetups around town; DevOpsDays Taipei and JCConf are the two I never miss.
        Hiked the 2026 Taipei Grand Trail (臺北大縱走).
      </p>
      <p>
        Code on <a href="https://github.com/kehao-chen" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>,
        work history on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kehao-chen/?locale=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>,
        half-thoughts on <a href="https://x.com/_hhnj" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">X</a>.
      </p>
    </TerminalWindow>
  </main>
</FrontLayout>
